<CapaProblem id="FormulaGraderDemo" title="Normalized Learning Gain">

<Markdown>
Variables:
* Let $S_i$ be the initial (pre-test) score on a scale from 0-1
* Let $S_j$ be the final (post-test) score

Hake (1998) used the *normalized learning gain* as the ratio of actual gain ($S_j-S_i$) to maximum possible gain ($1-S_i$) -- in other words, of the material the student didn't know going in, how much did they learn?

Write the formula for normalized gain.
</Markdown>

<FormulaGrader answer="(S_j - S_i) / (1 - S_i)" samples="S_i,S_j@0.1,0.2:0.8,0.95#10">
  <FormulaInput variables="S_i,S_j" placeholder="e.g. (S_j - S_i) / ..." />
</FormulaGrader>

</CapaProblem>
